{
  "runId": "skill-extension-audit-ms5ocpd3-zpl2zg",
  "workflowName": "skill-extension-audit",
  "script": "export const meta = {\n  name: \"skill-extension-audit\",\n  description: \"Audit pi harness skills and extensions for cohesion, redundancy, usefulness\",\n  phases: [{ title: \"cluster-audits\" }, { title: \"synthesis\" }]\n};\n\nconst SKILLS = \"/home/alex/.pi/agent/skills\";\nconst NM = \"/home/alex/.pi/agent/npm/node_modules\";\nconst REPO = \"/home/alex/Projects/pi-harness-config\";\nconst SUB = \"Lilac/moonshotai/kimi-k2.6\";\n\nconst COMMON = `You are auditing part of a pi (coding agent harness) config. Read the listed files with your tools (ctx_read/ctx_ls/ctx_grep). For EACH item report:\n- one-line purpose\n- how it activates (trigger word, auto, command, extension hook)\n- overlap with other items you saw (name them, rate overlap: none/partial/heavy)\n- verdict: KEEP / CUT / MERGE(into what) — one line why\nBe terse. Fragments fine. Under 500 words total. Ground every claim in a file you actually read; if a path is missing, say so and move on.`;\n\nconst auditors = [\n  {\n    label: \"workflow-orchestration\",\n    prompt: `${COMMON}\nYOUR CLUSTER: workflow orchestration. The user's #1 worry: do pi-dynamic-workflows and ce-lite conflict?\nRead:\n1. ${NM}/@quintinshaw/pi-dynamic-workflows/README.md and package.json (skim dist/workflow.ts only if README unclear)\n2. ${NM}/@quintinshaw/pi-dynamic-workflows/skills/ — list dirs, read workflow-patterns/SKILL.md (workflow-authoring already known: it's the authoring reference)\n3. ${SKILLS}/ce-lite/SKILL.md\n4. ${REPO}/skills/ce-lite/SKILL.md (repo copy — same or diverged?)\nAnswer specifically: Who decides when to call the workflow tool? Does ce-lite duplicate or delegate to pi-dynamic-workflows? Are workflow-authoring/workflow-patterns redundant with each other? Verdict on each of the 4 items.`\n  },\n  {\n    label: \"context-management\",\n    prompt: `${COMMON}\nYOUR CLUSTER: context/token management — the cluster with the most suspected redundancy (6+ tools).\nRead README.md + package.json of each extension in ${NM}: context-mode, pi-lean-ctx, pi-cache-graph, pi-cache-optimizer, pi-context-usage, pi-slim.\nAlso read:\n- ${NM}/context-mode/skills/ if it exists (ctx-doctor, ctx-index, ctx-insight, ctx-purge, ctx-search, ctx-stats, ctx-upgrade skills — read 2-3 SKILL.md files to characterize them)\n- ${NM}/@samfp/pi-essentials/src/image-context-pruner.ts and compact-header.ts (skim headers/comments)\n- ${REPO}/lean-ctx/config.toml, ${REPO}/pi-lean-ctx-config.json, ${REPO}/rules/lean-ctx.md\n- compaction block in ${REPO}/settings.json\nAnswer specifically: Which tools operate on the same layer (context pruning/compression/caching)? Do lean-ctx and context-mode do the same job? Does pi-cache-optimizer duplicate pi-cache-graph? Which 2-3 should survive? Verdict on each item.`\n  },\n  {\n    label: \"planning-pipeline\",\n    prompt: `${COMMON}\nYOUR CLUSTER: planning/annotation — user's worry #3: how does plannotator fit?\nRead:\n1. ${NM}/@plannotator/pi-extension/README.md + package.json\n2. SKILL.md of each: ${SKILLS}/to-spec, ${SKILLS}/to-questionnaire, ${SKILLS}/to-tickets, ${SKILLS}/codebase-design, ${SKILLS}/domain-modeling, ${SKILLS}/prototype, ${SKILLS}/implement, ${SKILLS}/tdd, ${SKILLS}/setup-ts-deep-modules\nAnswer specifically: Does plannotator (plan annotation UI) complement or compete with the to-spec→to-tickets→implement pipeline? Is to-questionnaire redundant with to-spec? Do codebase-design/domain-modeling/setup-ts-deep-modules overlap? Map the intended pipeline and flag breaks. Verdict on each item.`\n  },\n  {\n    label: \"research-cluster\",\n    prompt: `${COMMON}\nYOUR CLUSTER: research skills — heavy redundancy suspected (3 grilling skills!).\nRead SKILL.md of each: ${SKILLS}/research, ${SKILLS}/wayfinder, ${SKILLS}/ask-matt, ${SKILLS}/grill-me, ${SKILLS}/grill-with-docs, ${SKILLS}/grilling, ${SKILLS}/invest-optimizer, ${SKILLS}/calibrate-longevity.\nAlso:\n- ${NM}/pi-autoresearch/README.md + package.json, and its bundled skills autoresearch-create/finalize/hooks if present (check ${NM}/pi-autoresearch/skills/)\n- ${REPO}/skills/agents-skills/last30days/ — read its SKILL.md or README if present\n- skim ${REPO}/research/wayfinder/01-inventory-local-corpus.md (first 40 lines) to see if wayfinder research already concluded something about this stack\nAnswer specifically: grill-me vs grill-with-docs vs grilling — are 3 needed? research vs wayfinder vs autoresearch vs last30days — which trigger when? Are invest-optimizer/calibrate-longevity/ai-consultant-career personal-domain skills that belong in a different bucket? Verdict on each item.`\n  },\n  {\n    label: \"code-quality-process\",\n    prompt: `${COMMON}\nYOUR CLUSTER: code quality & process skills.\nRead SKILL.md of each: ${SKILLS}/code-review, ${SKILLS}/diagnosing-bugs, ${SKILLS}/improve-codebase-architecture, ${SKILLS}/no-ai-slop, ${SKILLS}/impeccable, ${SKILLS}/setup-matt-pocock-skills, ${SKILLS}/setup-pre-commit, ${SKILLS}/resolving-merge-conflicts, ${SKILLS}/handoff, ${SKILLS}/teach, ${SKILLS}/triage, ${SKILLS}/writing-great-skills, ${SKILLS}/ai-consultant-career.\nAlso read: ${NM}/pi-tscg/README.md + package.json, ${NM}/cc-safety-net/README.md + package.json, ${REPO}/tscg.json (first 30 lines).\nAnswer specifically: no-ai-slop vs impeccable vs code-review vs improve-codebase-architecture — how many quality gates does one harness need? Is handoff (skill) overlapping session features? Is ai-consultant-career a misfit in this harness? What does pi-tscg do that skills don't? Verdict on each item.`\n  },\n  {\n    label: \"extension-utility\",\n    prompt: `${COMMON}\nYOUR CLUSTER: utility extensions + dormant packages.\nENABLED (verify what each does — read source header comments or README):\n- ${NM}/@samfp/pi-essentials/src/: auto-session-name.ts, auto-title.ts, clipboard-image.ts, markdown-viewer.ts\n- ${NM}/pi-continue, ${NM}/pi-herdr-btw, ${NM}/@ogulcancelik/pi-model-agents, ${NM}/@ogulcancelik/pi-model-thinking — README + package.json each\nDORMANT (installed in node_modules but NOT in settings.json packages — just confirm each exists and one-line what it is from its package.json description):\npi-btw, pi-context-prune, pi-goal-list-loop-audit, pi-hermes-memory, pi-lens, pi-mcp-adapter, pi-readcache, pi-shazam, pi-simplify, pi-smart-compact, pi-subagents, pi-web-access, gentle-engram, @hypabolic/pi-hypa, @leing2021/super-pi, @narumitw/pi-goal, @ogulcancelik/pi-handoff, @ogulcancelik/pi-herdr, @ogulcancelik/pi-session-recall, @gotgenes/pi-permission-system\nAnswer specifically: auto-session-name vs auto-title — duplicates? pi-herdr-btw vs dormant pi-herdr vs pi-btw — same family, which is active? Which dormant packages shadow enabled functionality (e.g. pi-context-prune vs image-context-pruner, pi-smart-compact vs compaction settings)? Recommend: enable any dormant? uninstall which? Verdict per enabled item + a dormant summary table.`\n  },\n  {\n    label: \"harness-coherence\",\n    prompt: `${COMMON}\nYOUR CLUSTER: harness-level coherence — does the config itself create conflicts?\nRead:\n1. ${REPO}/settings.json, ${REPO}/models.json, ${REPO}/APPEND_SYSTEM.md\n2. ${REPO}/README.md, ${REPO}/WORKFLOW.md\n3. Compare repo skill copies vs installed: ${REPO}/skills/ has ce-lite, prompt-sharpen, agents-skills/{last30days,invest-optimizer,calibrate-longevity,ai-consultant-career,...}, mattpocock/* — check which also exist in ${SKILLS}/ (ce-lite, invest-optimizer, calibrate-longevity do). Are they symlinks, copies, diverged? (use ls -la / diff -q on ce-lite SKILL.md)\n4. Skim (first 50 lines each): ${REPO}/research/ce-upstream-radar.md, ${REPO}/research/cutting-edge-gap-analysis-2026-07-28.md, ${REPO}/research/progressive-disclosure-findings.md — do these already contain audit conclusions about this stack?\n5. ${REPO}/docs/agents/issue-tracker.md (first 50 lines)\nAnswer specifically: Is there a single source of truth for skills, or two divergent copies? Does APPEND_SYSTEM.md contradict any skill/extension behavior (e.g. session guardrail, output contract)? Do prior research docs already recommend cuts that weren't applied? Verdict: coherence risks list.`\n  }\n];\n\nphase(\"cluster-audits\");\nlog(\"fanning out \" + auditors.length + \" cluster auditors on kimi-k2.6\");\nconst results = await parallel(auditors.map(a => () => agent(a.prompt, { label: a.label, model: SUB })));\n\nphase(\"synthesis\");\nconst coverage = auditors.map((a, i) => ({ cluster: a.label, covered: results[i] !== null }));\nconst missing = coverage.filter(c => !c.covered).map(c => c.cluster);\nconst bundle = auditors.map((a, i) => `## CLUSTER: ${a.label}\\n${results[i] === null ? \"[MISSING — agent returned null]\" : results[i]}`).join(\"\\n\\n\");\n\nconst synthesis = await agent(`You are the lead auditor synthesizing a pi harness config audit. The user's core questions: (1) too many skills/extensions doing too many things — especially pi-dynamic-workflows vs ce-lite vs plannotator — how to know they work cohesively? (2) what is redundant? (3) what is useful?\n${missing.length ? \"NOTE: these clusters failed and must be flagged as UNAUDITED: \" + missing.join(\", \") : \"All 7 clusters reported.\"}\n\nCluster reports:\n${bundle}\n\nProduce the final audit report in Markdown, under 1200 words:\n1. **Cohesion verdict** — one paragraph: does the stack have an architecture or is it accreted? Specifically answer the dynamic-workflows/ce-lite/plannotator triangle: who orchestrates, who gates trivial questions, who renders plans — complementary or colliding?\n2. **Redundancy matrix** — table: Item | Overlaps with | Severity | Resolution (keep X, cut Y). Only real overlaps, ranked by severity.\n3. **Keep / Cut / Merge lists** — aggressive. The user wants fewer moving parts.\n4. **Dormant weight** — installed-but-disabled packages worth uninstalling.\n5. **Cohesion test** — 3-5 concrete checks the user can run to verify the pieces work together (e.g. trigger phrases to try, config files to diff).\nGround every claim in the cluster reports. No hedging.`, { label: \"synthesis\", model: SUB });\n\nreturn { coverage, synthesis };",
